# CAPTURE COST, cell A: the captured source is DEAD after the capture, so the
# capture MOVES and materialises nothing.
#
# `prefix`'s only mention after the capture is INSIDE the closure body, and a
# by-value capture reads the ENVIRONMENT FIELD there, not the outer local. So
# the outer local is dead at the capture and the ratified answer is
# move-if-it-is-dead: zero clones, and the two allocations are the two `mk`
# results.
#
# ⚠ THE INSTRUMENT IS `--clones=stats`, NOT stdout. This program prints
# `prefix!` whether the capture moves, clones, or (unsoundly) aliases — see
# `closure_capture_capture_cost_axis` in `tests/integration.rs`, which asserts
# both cells of the axis with exact equality.
#
# ⚠ ITS TWIN IS `closure_capture_live_source_clones.gg`, identical but for one
# extra read of `prefix` AFTER the capture. One fixture cannot pin this: a
# compiler that always clones passes the twin, and one that never clones passes
# this one and is unsound. The pair is the guard.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    String prefix = mk("pre", "fix")
    Callable[String()] f = (): mk(prefix, "!")
    print(f())
